+refuses that environment. Explicit empty strings are passed through. Missing
+files contribute nothing; invalid or unreadable files (including dangling links)
+fail. Both files are validated even when a machine lock suppresses an operator
+entry. `Files.Complete` finishes the section against the real tagged
+`agents-management` module (`v0.5.10` in `go.mod`): the `Lineup` leader
+supplies only unset members with its declared `Effort.Recommended` (or no
+effort for effortless rows), and an admittable nothing is
+`defaults_unresolvable` — the launcher never invents a model. The
+executable reads both files after mapping, refuses locked flags with
+`usage`, and prints the resolved pair with per-member origins on stderr
+before the plan request. The `pi-native` runtime is not declared by the
+pinned module yet, so `pi` without fully supplied files refuses; model
+admission and the plan request belong to the next milestone. Run
+`go test ./internal/defaults -count=1 -cover` for the filesystem,
+strict-schema, presence, lock, precedence, lineup, and line-group suite.
+Tests use temporary paths.
+
 Because no `ax.json` is read yet, the binary always parses as an untracked
 machine, so `--ax-profile` is currently always a usage error and `--name`
